  "title": "Failure, repair and termination",
  "takeaway": "Deterministic gates route repairable findings to D17, which plans a targeted repair and retests only the affected descendants; model faults are bounded at two attempts before CONVERGENCE_EXHAUSTED. M06 has no incoming edge in the compiled graph, so the model-repair arm of this loop cannot be entered.",
  "scope": "Compiled topology at 9ef14e8. D91 is also reached from M01\u2013M04, not only M05; every node in the graph carries its own edge to D98 and to D96 \u2014 only the decision-bearing ones are drawn.",
